        "comments": "The assembly dmBerAqui1.hap1.2 is based on 49x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The following regions of this assembly consist of scaffolds in an uncertain order and orientation: Chromosome 3\n35.5-43.9 Mbp, Chromosome 6\n41.5-56.8 Mbp, Chromosome 8\n31.6-39 Mbp, Chromosome 12\n30.9-35.3 Mbp and Chromosome 14\n16.4-23.7 Mbp. The following regions represent heterozygous inversions: Chromosome 1\n23.1-34.5 Mbp (multiple), Chromosome 7\n25-27 Mbp (single), Chromosome 9\n34.3-37.8 Mbp (double) and Chromosome 11\n27.3-29.7 (single) and\n44.3-47.1 Mbp (double)",
